Date: Wed, 1 Oct 2026 22:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] test: accept musl's dlerror() wording for a missing VM

evmc/vmtester/nonexistingvm checks that evmc-vmtester reports a failure when
asked to load a shared library that does not exist. The functional behaviour is
correct on every platform: dlopen() fails and the tool exits non-zero. The test
only asserts on the *text* of the diagnostic, with:

    PASS_REGULAR_EXPRESSION "[Cc]annot open|no such file"

That regex matches glibc's dlerror() text ("cannot open shared object file: No
such file or directory"). OpenHarmony uses musl, whose dlerror() reports the
raw strerror() string instead:

    Error loading shared library nonexistingvm: No such file or directory

The message differs only in capitalisation ("No such file" vs "no such file"),
so the lowercase alternative does not match and the test fails even though the
loader behaved correctly.

Fix: make the expected-regex alternatives case-insensitive with respect to the
first letter, i.e. "[Cc]annot open|[Nn]o such file". This keeps matching every
message the test matched before (glibc) and additionally matches the musl
wording.

This patch only widens the accepted diagnostic text. It does not change any
assertion about the tool's behaviour, nor any test input or expected exit code.
---
 test/vmtester/CMakeLists.txt | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/test/vmtester/CMakeLists.txt b/test/vmtester/CMakeLists.txt
--- a/test/vmtester/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/test/vmtester/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -13,7 +13,7 @@ add_test(NAME ${prefix}/help COMMAND evmc::evmc-vmtester --version --help)
 set_tests_properties(${prefix}/help PROPERTIES PASS_REGULAR_EXPRESSION "Usage:")
 
 add_test(NAME ${prefix}/nonexistingvm COMMAND evmc::evmc-vmtester nonexistingvm)
-set_tests_properties(${prefix}/nonexistingvm PROPERTIES PASS_REGULAR_EXPRESSION "[Cc]annot open|no such file")
+set_tests_properties(${prefix}/nonexistingvm PROPERTIES PASS_REGULAR_EXPRESSION "[Cc]annot open|[Nn]o such file")
 
 add_test(NAME ${prefix}/noarg COMMAND evmc::evmc-vmtester)
 set_tests_properties(${prefix}/noarg PROPERTIES PASS_REGULAR_EXPRESSION "is required")
